# The 5.1 GB OpenStax source. NEVER commit this path: it is untracked bulk data, and a
# symlink committed here was checked out over the real directory in the main worktree and
# destroyed it. Keep it ignored so `git add -A` cannot pick it up.
corpus/raw
build/model_*.bin
overnight.log
probe_*.txt
d2_*.txt

# figure-generation environment (paper/requirements-figures.txt)
paper/.venv-fig/

# paper build outputs (regenerable)
# paper/manuscript/paper.pdf and paper-arxiv.pdf ARE tracked: the folder is the deliverable.
paper/manuscript/*.aux
paper/manuscript/*.bbl
paper/manuscript/*.blg
paper/manuscript/*.log
paper/manuscript/*.out
paper/manuscript/paper-arxiv.tex
paper/manuscript/figures/*.png
paper/__pycache__/

# int8 exports for host scoring on the device decoder (regenerable)
build/int8/

# ---- 2026-09-26 tidy-up ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build/ holds what `make` produces. The few DATA files there stay tracked (model4096*.bin,
# tok4096.tok, tok_reference.json, transfer/README.txt): an ignore rule never untracks a tracked
# file, and a new data file needs `git add -f`.
build/*
# host tools compiled by `make` next to their sources
tools/eval/evalcli
tools/eval/provcli
tools/eval/shapecli
tools/eval/test_eval
# local leftovers, kept rather than deleted (attic/README.txt)
attic/
# model checkpoints are too large for git; train/README.md lists the ones that matter and must be
# backed up. Checkpoints tracked before this rule stay tracked.
train/*.pt
train/archive_*/
